src(s0).scale(1).thresh(0.4).modulate(src(s0).modulatePixelate(osc(0.1,0.1),100), 0.1).out(o0)


src(o0).modulate(src(o0), 0.3).add(src(o0).color(0,0,1).scrollX(0.2,0.4)).out(o1) 

src(o2).modulate(src(o0), 0.01).blend(noise(1000).color(0.7,0.6,0), 0.1).out(o2) // you can also invert the noise instead of the color, nice results too. Non inverted is just easier to read. Play with modulation amount also

solid(0.6,0.6,0.6).add(src(o2).scale(0.6).mask(shape(4, 0.6))).out(o3)


